~ start
Mira: Welcome. This is the first playable slice of GameBase.
- What can I do here?
	Mira: Walk around, approach me, and press E to interact. The next systems will build on this same interaction layer.
	=> start
- Why does the menu look different from the world?
	Mira: The menu comes from the preserved Godot-GameTemplate foundation. The game-specific layer is kept separate so we can upgrade or replace systems cleanly.
	=> start
- See you later.
	Mira: See you around.
	=> END

~ friend_2
Mira: You have become part of the rhythm around here. I notice when the farm is quiet now.
- Anything I can help with?

Mira: Keep an eye on the weather. A rainy morning can save you a surprising amount of work.

=> END
- I will see you around.

Mira: I am counting on it.

=> END

~ friend_4
Mira: I used to think of your farm as the new place outside town. Now it just feels like part of home.
- That means a lot.

Mira: Good. I meant it.

=> END
- You are getting sentimental.

Mira: Do not get used to it.

=> END

~ heart_2
Mira: I saved some time for you. Walk with me for a minute?
Mira: When you first arrived, I expected another person who would rush through a season and disappear.
Mira: You stayed, helped people, and actually learned how this place works. I am glad I was wrong.
- I am glad I stayed too.

Mira: Then keep staying.

=> END
- I still have a lot to learn.

Mira: That is probably why you fit in.

=> END

~ friend_6
Mira: I started leaving a little space in the garden plan for whatever strange crop you decide to bring home next.
- You plan around me now?
	Mira: Around your surprises. There is a difference.
	=> END
- I will try to make it worth the space.
	Mira: You usually do.
	=> END

~ friend_8
Mira: When I set aside good seed now, I catch myself wondering what you would grow with it.
- Save me the difficult ones.
	Mira: I knew you would say that.
	=> END
- Keep some for yourself too.
	Mira: That is why I trust you with the rest.
	=> END

~ friend_10
Mira: I used to measure seasons by planting dates. Lately I measure them by who I expect to still be here when they change.
- I am not going anywhere.
	Mira: Good. Neither am I.
	=> END

~ heart_4
Mira: Look at the garden beds now. Before the restoration, half of this ground was giving up.
Mira: You did more than donate materials. You convinced people the place was worth investing in again.
- The town did the work together.
	Mira: Exactly. You are learning what makes a place last.
	=> END
- I just wanted the garden back.
	Mira: Practical motives can still grow into something bigger.
	=> END

~ heart_6
Mira: Funny meeting you in Riverside. A year ago these towns felt farther apart than the road says they are.
Mira: Now I hear your name here almost as often as back home.
- I like having reasons to cross the bridge.
	Mira: Then keep making good ones.
	=> END
- Maybe the valley is getting smaller.
	Mira: Or our idea of home is getting larger.
	=> END

~ heart_8
Mira: People ask me what you think before they start new work now.
Mira: I hope you realize that trust is heavier than praise. You have to keep carrying it after everyone stops clapping.
- I can carry it.
	Mira: I know. That is why I said it to you.
	=> END

~ heart_10
Mira: The three towns are arguing about ordinary things again. That is how I know the rebuilding worked.
Mira: No emergency meetings, no broken routes. Just people planning next season.
- What are you planning?
	Mira: A garden with enough room for whatever comes next. I already saved you a row.
	=> END
